5.Compare your procedural C version and OOP TaskList version: List 3 problems you faced in the C version that were solved by using classes and methods in the OOP version.

C Version Problem	

1. We need separate arrays for task names and their status.	
2. Functions and data are separate, so managing many tasks becomes harder.	
3. Adding and managing many tasks requires more manual code.	

How OOP Solves It

1.The Task class keeps title and isDone together in one object.
2. Methods like markDone() and display() belong directly to the Task object.
3. TaskList can store many Task objects and provides simple methods like addTask() and markTaskDone().